# AICL Example: Robotics Controller
# Advanced robotics controller with motion planning, multi-sensor fusion, inverse kinematics,
# safety stop systems, and hierarchical task sequencing for industrial and service robots.

Goal: Build a robotics controller that provides smooth motion planning with collision avoidance,
    multi-sensor fusion for precise localization, real-time inverse kinematics for multi-DOF
    manipulators, failsafe stop mechanisms, and hierarchical task sequencing for complex operations.

Constraint: Motion planning must generate collision-free trajectories within 10ms for 6-DOF
    manipulators with joint velocity and acceleration limits enforced at all times.

Constraint: Sensor fusion must produce localization estimate within 1mm position accuracy and
    0.1 degree orientation accuracy at 1kHz update rate for precision tasks.

Constraint: Inverse kinematics solver must converge within 1ms for 6-DOF manipulators with
    singularity handling and joint limit avoidance in the solution space.

Constraint: Safety stops must halt all motion within 50ms of trigger with category 3 stop
    per ISO 13850 and safe torque off per IEC 61800-5-2 for all drive axes.

Constraint: Task sequencer must support preemptive priority-based scheduling with guaranteed
    completion of safety-critical tasks regardless of lower-priority task state.

Risk: Collision between robot arm and workspace obstacle during motion execution
Recovery: Emergency stop all axes within 50ms; retract along collision-free path computed
    from last known safe configuration; log collision event with full state snapshot

Risk: Inverse kinematics singularity causes uncontrollable joint velocities
Recovery: Detect singularity proximity through manipulability measure; apply damped least
    squares with adaptive damping factor; reduce task speed near singular configurations

Risk: Sensor fusion divergence produces incorrect localization estimate
Recovery: Detect divergence through innovation filter monitoring; fall back to last
    convergent estimate; reduce motion speed; attempt sensor recalibration sequence

Risk: Safety stop system fails to halt motion on demand
Recovery: Implement dual-channel safety architecture with hardwired safety relay; monitor
    safety PLC response time; activate mechanical brake if electrical stop fails

Risk: Task sequencing deadlock prevents robot from completing operations
Recovery: Detect deadlock through resource dependency cycle analysis; apply deadlock
    resolution protocol with priority preemption; log deadlock for sequence optimization

Risk: Joint limit violation during high-speed motion exceeds mechanical bounds
Recovery: Apply soft joint limits with deceleration zone before hard stop; enforce velocity
    reduction within 5 degrees of joint limit; emergency stop on hard limit contact

Layer: RoboticsController
    SubLayer: MotionPlanning
    SubLayer: SensorFusion
    SubLayer: InverseKinematics
    SubLayer: SafetySystem
    SubLayer: TaskSequencer

Validation: All motion trajectories must be collision-free before execution
Validation: Inverse kinematics solution must satisfy all joint limits and velocity constraints
Validation: Sensor fusion estimate must include covariance matrix for uncertainty quantification
Validation: Safety stop must achieve zero velocity within 50ms on all axes
Validation: Task sequences must be validated for deadlock-free execution before start
Validation: Joint positions must never exceed hard mechanical limits under any condition
Validation: Controller must maintain heartbeat with safety PLC at 1kHz minimum

# Level 2: Entities

Entity RobotArm
    arm_id: string
    dof: integer
    joint_positions: list
    joint_velocities: list
    joint_limits_min: list
    joint_limits_max: list
    max_velocities: list
    max_accelerations: list
    payload_kg: float

Entity Trajectory
    trajectory_id: string
    arm_id: string
    waypoints: list
    duration_s: float
    is_collision_free: boolean
    interpolation_type: string
    created_at: datetime

Entity FusionEstimate
    estimate_id: string
    position: dict
    orientation: dict
    covariance: list
    sensor_contributions: dict
    innovation: dict
    is_converged: boolean
    timestamp: datetime

Entity IKSolution
    solution_id: string
    arm_id: string
    target_pose: dict
    joint_angles: list
    manipulability: float
    singularity_proximity: float
    computation_time_ms: float
    is_valid: boolean

Entity SafetyState
    robot_id: string
    stop_category: integer
    is_stopped: boolean
    stop_reason: string
    safety_plc_heartbeat: datetime
    drive_safe_torque_off: list
    mechanical_brake_engaged: list
    recovery_required: boolean

Entity TaskSequence
    sequence_id: string
    robot_id: string
    tasks: list
    current_task_index: integer
    resource_locks: dict
    priority: integer
    is_preemptible: boolean
    status: string

# Level 3: Behaviors

Behavior PlanMotion
    Input:
        arm_id: string
        target_pose: dict
        constraints: dict
        obstacle_map: dict
    Output:
        trajectory: dict
        is_collision_free: boolean
        planning_time_ms: float
    Action:
        Transform target pose to joint-space goal configuration
        Search configuration space using RRT* or trajectory optimization
        Check collision along candidate trajectories against obstacle map
        Apply time-optimal trajectory parameterization with jerk limits
        Validate against all joint velocity and acceleration constraints
        Return collision-free trajectory or failure with replanning suggestion

Behavior FuseSensors
    Input:
        joint_encoders: list
        force_torque: dict
        vision_pose: dict
        imu_data: dict
    Output:
        fused_estimate: dict
        covariance: list
        is_converged: boolean
    Action:
        Predict state using robot kinematic model
        Update prediction with each sensor measurement sequentially
        Apply innovation filter to detect and reject outlier measurements
        Compute fused estimate with full covariance propagation
        Check convergence criterion on innovation sequence
        Monitor individual sensor health and exclude degraded sensors

Behavior SolveIK
    Input:
        arm_id: string
        target_pose: dict
        current_joints: list
        nullspace_objective: string
    Output:
        joint_angles: list
        manipulability: float
        singularity_proximity: float
    Action:
        Compute Jacobian at current configuration
        Apply damped least squares with adaptive damping near singularities
        Project nullspace component for secondary optimization objective
        Iterate until convergence or maximum iteration count
        Validate solution against joint limits and velocity constraints
        Compute manipulability and singularity proximity metrics

Behavior ExecuteSafetyStop
    Input:
        stop_category: integer
        stop_reason: string
        current_state: dict
    Output:
        stop_achieved: boolean
        time_to_stop_ms: float
        axes_stopped: list
    Action:
        Determine stop category and corresponding deceleration profile
        Apply deceleration ramp to all moving axes simultaneously
        Activate safe torque off on drives once velocity reaches zero
        Engage mechanical brakes for holding position
        Confirm stop through dual-channel safety PLC verification
        Log stop event with full state and timing information

Behavior SequenceTasks
    Input:
        sequence_id: string
        task_list: list
        resource_requirements: dict
        priority: integer
    Output:
        execution_order: list
        resource_schedule: dict
        estimated_duration_s: float
    Action:
        Analyze task dependencies and resource requirements
        Build execution graph with partial ordering constraints
        Detect and resolve potential deadlocks through cycle analysis
        Schedule tasks with priority-based preemptive policy
        Allocate resource locks with deadlock prevention protocol
        Execute tasks sequentially with parallelism where dependencies allow

# Level 4: Conditions

Condition: CollisionDetected
    When planned trajectory intersects with obstacle in workspace
    Then abort trajectory execution immediately, retract to last safe
        configuration, and trigger replanning with updated obstacle map

Condition: SingularityApproaching
    When manipulability measure drops below threshold indicating singularity proximity
    Then increase damping factor in IK solver, reduce motion speed proportionally,
        and consider alternative IK solution with better manipulability

Condition: FusionDivergence
    When innovation filter Mahalanobis distance exceeds 3-sigma threshold
    Then flag sensor fusion as diverged, fall back to last convergent estimate,
        reduce motion speed, and initiate sensor diagnostic sequence

Condition: SafetyStopTriggered
    When safety PLC commands stop or emergency stop button activated
    Then execute category 3 stop on all axes within 50ms, engage mechanical
        brakes, and prevent any motion until safety reset with authorization

Condition: JointLimitApproaching
    When any joint position is within 5 degrees of soft joint limit
    Then reduce velocity proportionally to distance from limit, apply
        deceleration profile, and emergency stop if hard limit contacted

Condition: TaskDeadlineMissed
    When task execution exceeds allocated time budget by more than 20 percent
    Then escalate task priority, preempt lower-priority tasks for resource
        access, and alert operator if deadline cannot be recovered

# Level 5: Events

Event: TrajectoryCompleted
    On motion_planning_execution_finished_successfully
    Action: Update robot state with final configuration, release trajectory
        resources, and signal task sequencer to advance to next task

Event: IKSolutionFound
    On inverse_kinematics_solver_converged
    Action: Validate solution against all constraints, forward to motion
        planner for trajectory generation, and update manipulability metrics

Event: SafetyStopActivated
    On safety_stop_condition_triggered
    Action: Log stop event with full context, notify task sequencer to pause
        all tasks, and require safety reset before motion can resume

Event: SensorRecalibrated
    On sensor_fusion_recovers_from_divergence
    Action: Validate new calibration against ground truth, resume high-speed
        motion if within accuracy specification, and log recalibration event

Event: TaskCompleted
    On task_sequence_step_finished
    Action: Release resource locks, update task status, and advance to next
        task in sequence or signal sequence completion to coordinator

# Level 6: Concurrency

Parallel:
    Motion planning with trajectory optimization
    Sensor fusion running at 1kHz update rate
    Inverse kinematics computation for trajectory waypoints
    Safety PLC communication and stop monitoring
    Task execution and resource management
    Joint limit monitoring on all axes
    Collision checking against workspace obstacle map

# Level 7: Optimization

Optimize: Motion execution speed while maintaining safety and precision
    Priority: Safety stop responsiveness takes absolute precedence over all motion goals
    Priority: Collision avoidance is mandatory; no trajectory executed without clearance check
    Priority: Joint limit avoidance preferred over task speed near mechanical bounds
    Priority: Trajectory smoothness optimized for minimum jerk within time constraints
    Priority: Task throughput maximized subject to safety and precision constraints

# Level 8: Learning

Learn: Optimal trajectory parameters for common motion patterns
    Goal: Reduce average task cycle time by 20% while maintaining precision
    Adapt: Trajectory waypoint positions and timing profiles
        Based: Historical execution times, vibration measurements, and precision outcomes

Learn: Sensor fusion noise characteristics per operating condition
    Goal: Improve localization accuracy to 0.5mm under varying conditions
    Adapt: Process and measurement noise covariance matrices per sensor
        Based: Innovation sequence statistics, temperature, and vibration environment data

Learn: Task sequence optimization for throughput
    Goal: Minimize idle time and resource contention across task sequences
    Adapt: Task ordering and resource allocation strategies
        Based: Historical execution times, resource contention patterns, and deadline compliance

# Level 9: Security

Security:
    Encrypt: All safety PLC communication using authenticated safety protocols
    Encrypt: Controller-to-robot communication using TLS with hardware security module
    Protect: Safety configuration with dual-authorization modification requirement
    Protect: IK solution integrity with checksum verification before execution
    Protect: Task sequence definitions with signed authorization and change tracking
    Encrypt: Sensor data channels using AES-256 with per-session key derivation

# Level 10: Native

Native: C++
{
#include <vector>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <chrono>
#include <mutex>
#include <Eigen/Dense>

using Vector6d = Eigen::Matrix<double, 6, 1>;
using Matrix6d = Eigen::Matrix<double, 6, 6>;
using VectorXd = Eigen::VectorXd;
using MatrixXd = Eigen::MatrixXd;

struct JointLimits {
    Vector6d min_pos;
    Vector6d max_pos;
    Vector6d max_vel;
    Vector6d max_acc;
};

struct RobotPose {
    Eigen::Vector3d position;
    Eigen::Quaterniond orientation;
};

class DampedLeastSquaresIK {
private:
    double lambda_min_;
    double lambda_max_;
    double manipulability_threshold_;
    int max_iterations_;
    double position_tolerance_;
    double orientation_tolerance_;
    JointLimits limits_;

public:
    DampedLeastSquaresIK(double lam_min, double lam_max,
                          double manip_thresh, int max_iter,
                          double pos_tol, double ori_tol,
                          const JointLimits& limits)
        : lambda_min_(lam_min), lambda_max_(lam_max),
          manipulability_threshold_(manip_thresh),
          max_iterations_(max_iter),
          position_tolerance_(pos_tol),
          orientation_tolerance_(ori_tol),
          limits_(limits) {}

    struct IKResult {
        Vector6d joint_angles;
        double manipulability;
        double singularity_proximity;
        double computation_time_ms;
        bool is_valid;
        int iterations;
    };

    IKResult solve(const RobotPose& target,
                   const Vector6d& current_joints,
                   const std::function<Matrix6d(const Vector6d&)>& jacobian_fn,
                   const std::function<RobotPose(const Vector6d&)>& fk_fn) {
        auto start = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();
        IKResult result;
        result.joint_angles = current_joints;
        result.is_valid = false;
        result.iterations = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < max_iterations_; ++i) {
            result.iterations = i + 1;
            RobotPose current = fk_fn(result.joint_angles);
            Vector6d error = compute_error(target, current);

            if (error.head<3>().norm() < position_tolerance_ &&
                error.tail<3>().norm() < orientation_tolerance_) {
                result.is_valid = true;
                break;
            }

            Matrix6d J = jacobian_fn(result.joint_angles);
            double manip = std::sqrt((J * J.transpose()).determinant());
            result.manipulability = manip;

            double lambda = compute_damping(manip);
            result.singularity_proximity = 1.0 - manip / manipulability_threshold_;

            Matrix6d damped = J.transpose() * (J * J.transpose() +
                            lambda * lambda * Matrix6d::Identity()).inverse();
            Vector6d delta_q = damped * error;

            result.joint_angles += delta_q;

            for (int j = 0; j < 6; ++j) {
                result.joint_angles(j) = std::clamp(
                    result.joint_angles(j),
                    limits_.min_pos(j) + 0.01,
                    limits_.max_pos(j) - 0.01
                );
            }
        }

        auto end = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();
        result.computation_time_ms =
            std::chrono::duration<double, std::milli>(end - start).count();
        return result;
    }

private:
    double compute_damping(double manipulability) const {
        if (manipulability > manipulability_threshold_) {
            return lambda_min_;
        }
        double ratio = manipulability / manipulability_threshold_;
        return lambda_min_ + (lambda_max_ - lambda_min_) * (1.0 - ratio * ratio);
    }

    Vector6d compute_error(const RobotPose& target,
                           const RobotPose& current) const {
        Vector6d err;
        err.head<3>() = target.position - current.position;
        Eigen::AngleAxisd aa(target.orientation * current.orientation.inverse());
        err.tail<3>() = aa.angle() * aa.axis();
        return err;
    }
};

class SafetyMonitor {
private:
    std::mutex mutex_;
    int stop_category_;
    bool is_stopped_;
    std::chrono::system_clock::time_point stop_timestamp_;
    JointLimits limits_;

public:
    SafetyMonitor(const JointLimits& limits)
        : stop_category_(0), is_stopped_(false), limits_(limits) {}

    bool check_joint_limits(const Vector6d& joints) const {
        for (int i = 0; i < 6; ++i) {
            if (joints(i) <= limits_.min_pos(i) ||
                joints(i) >= limits_.max_pos(i)) {
                return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }

    bool check_velocity_limits(const Vector6d& velocities) const {
        for (int i = 0; i < 6; ++i) {
            if (std::abs(velocities(i)) > limits_.max_vel(i)) {
                return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }

    void trigger_stop(int category, const std::string& reason) {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
        stop_category_ = category;
        is_stopped_ = true;
        stop_timestamp_ = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
    }

    bool is_stopped() const {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
        return is_stopped_;
    }

    void reset_stop() {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
        is_stopped_ = false;
        stop_category_ = 0;
    }
};
}
